      "Gist": "The only production caller is POST /cart/discount, through `applyDiscount`. The check calls `Subtotal()`, and if the cart is short the handler returns 422. Nothing checks the minimum again after the code is applied.",
      "Detail": "**Test callers:**\n- `cart/discount_test.go:21` (case \"below the minimum\") expects `ErrBelowMinimum` and an unchanged total.\n- `server/server_test.go:78` expects 422 for BOOKWORM20 on a cart below the minimum.\n\n**Gap:** this is the only place the minimum is checked. `Savings` (`cart/cart.go:100-105`) and `Total` (`cart/cart.go:109-113`) apply the stored code without checking again. `Remove` (`cart/cart.go:46-53`) doesn't clear it either. So if items are removed after a code is applied, the cart keeps the discount even when it drops below the minimum.\n\nA rejected code also leaves any earlier code on the cart, because the function returns before `c.discount = \u0026d` (`cart/cart.go:87`).",
